---
/**
 * The single mount point for the live editor-widget demos in the docs.
 *
 * Render this once on a page and it registers <nr-typed-input> and
 * <nr-auto-complete> and brings in their styles plus the demo frame. The
 * elements themselves are then written as plain HTML, which is what makes them
 * usable from a Starlight markdown page: markdown can contain custom element
 * tags, but it cannot import an Astro component.
 *
 * WHY A COMPONENT AND NOT A FILE IN public/. The three pages that need this used
 * to pull their widgets from public/js/ with hand-written <script src> tags. That
 * is the arrangement being removed: unbundled, unhashed, unversioned, and
 * invisible to the build, which is how the site ended up serving a copy of
 * typedInput.js several hundred lines behind the editor without anything
 * noticing. Going through a component means Astro bundles and fingerprints both
 * modules, only the pages that render it pay for them, and a broken import is a
 * build failure rather than a 404 at runtime.
 *
 * WHY A CUSTOM ELEMENT AND NOT A FRAMEWORK ISLAND. The site ships no client
 * framework and no client router: navigations are native cross-document view
 * transitions (see src/styles/view-transition-head.js). A custom element needs no
 * hydration directive, initialises from customElements.define on script
 * evaluation, and comes up again on its own in every arriving document, because
 * every arriving document is a real document.
 *
 * HOW A MARKDOWN PAGE GETS IT. Markdown cannot render this, so a Starlight
 * override has to. Gate it on the route in src/components/starlight/PageFrame.astro
 * so only the widget pages load it:
 *
 *   const WIDGET_PAGES = new Set([
 *     '/docs/api/ui/typedInput/',
 *     '/docs/api/ui/autoComplete/',
 *     '/docs/creating-nodes/edit-dialog/',
 *   ]);
 *   ...
 *   {WIDGET_PAGES.has(Astro.url.pathname) && <DocsWidgets />}
 *
 * Astro deduplicates the hoisted script, so rendering it more than once on a page
 * is harmless.
 */
---

<script>
  import './nr-typed-input.js';
  import './nr-auto-complete.js';
  import './demo-frame.css';
  import './nr-editor-button.css';
</script>
